WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.708
This practice turns bookstore business rules into

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:07.116
constraints Customer email must be present and

00:00:07.142 --> 00:00:09.418
unique so think about the combination of

00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:13.706
NOT NULL and UNIQUE Order-item quantity must

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:15.772
be positive which is a CHECK rule

00:00:17.515 --> 00:00:19.804
Unit price cannot be negative which is

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.077
another CHECK Every order item must reference

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.353
an existing order and book so foreign

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.951
keys are required Deletion behavior depends on

00:00:30.977 --> 00:00:34.151
meaning Order items may cascade when their

00:00:34.177 --> 00:00:36.348
order is deleted while deleting a book

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:38.467
that appears in historical orders may need

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.405
to be restricted Try naming the constraint

00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:44.234
type for each rule before opening the

00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:47.907
sample patterns The important skill is translating

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.552
business language into database-enforced rules
